{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3","language":"python"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"thermal_sar":{"schema_version":"1.0","stage":"configuration_only"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":22472557}],"dockerImageVersionId":28755,"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false},"colab":{"name":"01_Research_Configuration_and_Environment.ipynb","provenance":[]}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"d79bd3fc","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Cell 1 — Research configuration and environment\n\n**Occlusion- and Uncertainty-Aware Real-Time Human Detection and Tracking in Thermal\nImagery from Unmanned Aerial Vehicles for Search and Rescue**\n\nThis PhD project studies anonymous human detection in aerial thermal imagery for civilian\nsearch and rescue. Small apparent targets, occlusion, and domain shifts motivate controlled\nexperiments. The title states the research objective; real-time performance and improved\naccuracy remain unproven. Identification, weapon detection, hostile-person classification,\nand targeting are outside scope. Thermal-only inference is the primary setting.\n\n**Purpose:** establish the research protocol, explicit baseline, configuration, and\nreproducibility records before reading annotations or training.\n\n**Inputs/dependencies:** this notebook, `src/config.py`, `src/reproducibility.py`, and\n`configs/base.yaml`; Python 3.11+ with PyYAML and nbformat. Torch, torchvision, NumPy,\nPillow, and pycocotools are inspected for future readiness. No dataset is required here.\n\n**Outputs:** a unique experiment directory containing effective configuration and its\nSHA-256, environment and baseline-source records, package inventory, seed settings,\ndependency readiness, source-file hashes, and a run manifest. No detector is built and\nno performance results are produced. Runtime category: **environment smoke test**.\n\nRun all cells in order from a fresh kernel. Shared code and configuration must be available\nalongside the notebook, locally or as an attached Kaggle code dataset. Cell 6 discovers\nthose files; explicit hints resolve ambiguous mount names.","metadata":{"id":"d79bd3fc"}},{"id":"d61e22ef","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cell 2 — Research questions and testable hypotheses\n\n1. Does a high-resolution pathway improve recall for small persons relative to the unmodified\n   detector under the same splits, training budget, input policy, and pretraining?\n2. Does image-dependent adaptive multi-scale fusion outperform fixed fusion and globally\n   learned static weights? Compare AP and subgroup recall across completed seeds.\n3. Does masked visibility supervision improve detection of genuinely occluded persons where\n   valid annotations exist? Report annotation counts and agreement before training this head.\n4. Do localization distributions and held-out confidence calibration improve appropriate\n   likelihood/coverage diagnostics and calibration under the frozen matching protocol?\n5. What accuracy, memory, and end-to-end latency trade-offs are observed on measured hardware?\n\nEach is a falsifiable hypothesis, including the possibility of no benefit or degraded results.\nMetadata, temporal processing, and identity metrics require verified supporting data.","metadata":{"id":"d61e22ef"}},{"id":"33922bfb","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cell 3 — Proposed contributions and established baseline\n\nThe primary hypothesis is **input-dependent adaptive multi-scale feature fusion with\nhigh-resolution features and auxiliary visibility supervision**. Reliability gating,\nprobabilistic localization, held-out calibration, metadata, temporal fusion, tracking,\nand deployment are later investigations. All switches are disabled in this notebook.\n\n**Concrete reference:** `torchvision.models.detection.fcos_resnet50_fpn`, the established\nFCOS detector with ResNet-50 and FPN. Its source has separable `backbone.body`,\n`backbone.fpn`, and `head` interfaces. The inspected torchvision 0.22.1 implementation\nreturns ResNet layers `[2, 3, 4]` (C3–C5), produces 256-channel P3–P5, and adds\nP6–P7 with `LastLevelP6P7(256, 256)`: nominal strides 8, 16, 32, 64, 128.\nIt does not include P2. These source-derived properties motivate testing a finer pathway;\nthey do not establish that it will help. Cell 7 records the implementation installed at run time.\n\nFCOS is anchor-free in formulation; torchvision uses one anchor-like reference point per\nlocation for assignment and box decoding. Its head includes classification, regression,\nand centerness, so the eventual reference loss includes centerness as well.\nInspect actual tensors and run forward/backward tests in Notebook 06 before modifying it.\n\n**Thermal input proposal:** repeat a decoded single thermal channel three times to retain\nthe reference encoder. This uses no RGB measurements. Confirm bit depth, intensity scaling,\nand normalization in Notebooks 02/05; thermal values are not assumed to be temperatures.\nProvisional resize settings retain the factory's 800-pixel short-side / 1333-pixel long-side\npolicy, not a fixed square. Freeze that choice after validation, before final-test inspection.\n\nCOCO_V1 weights are accessible upstream and proposed for the later baseline. Here the actual\nweight source is `none`; downloads are disabled. A configured local file can be validated\nwithout loading it. Notebook 06 must document state-dict compatibility, person-class mapping,\nhead adaptation, preprocessing, and all pretraining differences. Torchvision code is BSD-3-Clause;\ndataset and pretrained-weight terms require their own review. The detection API is marked beta.\n\nPrimary sources:\n- [FCOS source for torchvision v0.22.1](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/v0.22.1/torchvision/models/detection/fcos.py)\n- [Backbone/FPN source](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/v0.22.1/torchvision/models/detection/backbone_utils.py)\n- [Factory and weights documentation](https://docs.pytorch.org/vision/stable/generated/torchvision.models.detection.fcos_resnet50_fpn.html)\n- [Torchvision code license](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/blob/main/LICENSE)\n- [Reference detection evaluator](https://github.com/pytorch/vision/tree/v0.22.1/references/detection)\n- [HIT-UAV source and annotation description](https://github.com/suojiashun/HIT-UAV-Infrared-Thermal-Dataset)\n- [HIT-UAV license](https://github.com/suojiashun/HIT-UAV-Infrared-Thermal-Dataset/blob/main/LICENSE)\n\nHIT-UAV is the initial candidate dataset. Its upstream description includes standard and\noriented boxes and collection-condition information; this does not prove that a mounted\ncopy contains verified per-image metadata. Verify the actual version, labels, official\nsplits, and license in Notebook 02. MONET/WiSARD external evaluation and BIRDSAI/video\ntracking remain conditional on source and local-data inspection. No dataset is downloaded.","metadata":{"id":"33922bfb"}},{"id":"01185495","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cell 4 — Evaluation protocol and metrics\n\n**Primary:** person AP averaged over IoU 0.50:0.05:0.95 using one consistent COCO-style\nevaluator. Also report AP50 and person recall at a development-validation-selected score\nthreshold. Report false positives per evaluated image (FP/image), including empty scenes;\ndo not confuse this denominator with FP/(FP+TN), whose detection TN population is undefined.\n\nReport target-size groups in **original-image coordinates**; freeze category cutoffs during\ndata analysis. Visibility/altitude/day–night groups require verified labels and sample counts.\nPreserve official benchmark splits, and report additional research splits separately.\nAudit duplicates and candidate near-duplicates; use flight/sequence/location disjointness\nonly with verified groups. Keep training, development validation, held-out calibration,\ninternal test, and external test distinct. No final-test labels guide model selection,\npreprocessing statistics, calibration, thresholds, or hyperparameters.\n\n**Secondary, when implemented:** calibration error and reliability curves under explicit\ndetection matching/population rules; localization NLL and coverage; HOTA/IDF1/switches/\nfragmentation only with ground-truth identities. Anonymous tracker IDs are not person identity.\nRepeat principal comparisons across seeds where feasible, report actual runs, and resample\nverified groups rather than correlated frames as independent observations.\n\nMeasure batch-one latency with warm-up, GPU synchronization when applicable, median/tail\nlatency, memory, and separate preprocessing/model/postprocessing/tracking times. CPU, Kaggle\nGPU, and actual embedded-device results remain distinct. Model FPS alone does not prove\nend-to-end real-time operation. No metrics, confidence intervals, or energy measurements exist yet.","metadata":{"id":"01185495"}},{"id":"d5f503b9","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Cell 5 — Stages, dependencies, and artifact contracts\n\n| Stage | Notebooks | Entry requirement |\n|---|---|---|\n| Configuration | **01 (this notebook only)** | Shared source and base configuration |\n| Audit, visibility, splits, loaders | 02–05 | Mounted data and verified provenance |\n| A: unmodified baseline | 06 | Frozen splits, tested transforms/loaders |\n| B–D: high resolution, adaptive fusion, visibility | 07–10 | Working baseline and valid supervision |\n| E: probabilistic localization and calibration | 08–12 | Tested loss and separate calibration data |\n| F: optional metadata | 07/10 | Verified metadata plus tested missing-data fallback |\n| G: temporal processing/tracking | 13 | Causal sequences; identities for identity metrics |\n| Failure analysis, deployment, statistics, packaging | 14–17 | Frozen protocol and real completed runs |\n\nRun Notebook 01 independently from a fresh kernel. Later notebooks must load saved contracts,\nnever inherit variables. Approval is required before beginning Notebook 02. No training occurs here.\n\nDraft manifest contracts are recorded as version identifiers only in `config.contracts`:\nimage rows will contain dataset/image IDs, image path, dimensions, split, verified grouping\nIDs, optional camera/altitude fields, and availability indicators; object rows will contain\ndataset/image IDs, optional source object IDs, original/mapped class, xyxy coordinates,\noptional visibility and availability flag, and track IDs only when ground truth exists.\nMissing values remain null/masked. Row validators and real manifests belong to Notebook 02.\nThe split identifier/fingerprint remain null until real split contents are frozen in Notebook 04.\nA configuration hash is not a dataset checksum or split fingerprint.","metadata":{"id":"d5f503b9"}},{"id":"c5cc1084-37bf-44ce-b7ee-f59d2a8e02b3","cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nproject_root = Path(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/dule11/thermal-project-root\")\nrequired = [\"src/config.py\", \"src/reproducibility.py\", \"configs/base.yaml\"]\n\nmissing = [name for name in required if not (project_root / name).is_file()]\nif missing:\n    raise FileNotFoundError(f\"Missing project files: {missing}\")\n\nos.environ[\"THERMAL_PROJECT_ROOT\"] = str(project_root)\nprint(\"Verified project root:\", project_root)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T02:28:06.408788Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T02:28:06.409042Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T02:28:06.97396Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-20T02:28:06.409015Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T02:28:06.973183Z"},"id":"c5cc1084-37bf-44ce-b7ee-f59d2a8e02b3","outputId":"0ac8d46e-2c7b-40c4-9159-b3fa7488d9c0"},"outputs":[{"na